Author: Elliot <zhazhahui1806@gmail.com>
Date:   Sat Sep 12 13:48:11 2026 +0800

    fix(sb16): disarm dormant capture/playback engine on same dma channel

    Root cause:
    ALSA's arecord finishes capture by issuing DSP 0xD5 (pause), never 0xD9
    (exit), leaving the capture engine latched on DMA channel 5. Subsequent
    aplay on the same channel issues DSP 0xD6 (continue 16-bit), reviving the
    dormant capture engine. Interleaved parasitic capture cycles steal half
    the DMA periods (halving duration and sample count) and corrupt audio.

    Fix:
    - In vendor/v86 src/sb16.js: Add symmetric teardown guards in
      dma_transfer_start() and adc_transfer_start() when another transfer engine
      is already armed on the same DMA channel.
    - In tests/test-playback-probe.mjs: Update the previous KNOWN-DEFECT
      assertions (which pinned the bug's broken behavior) to assert normal
      playback ratio (≈1.0) and full sample delivery, now that the underlying
      defect is verified fixed.
    - Add regression test tests/test-sb16-dma-channel-reuse.mjs to verify
      playback duration, sample delivery, speed ratio, zero parasitic cycles,
      and disarmed engine state across arecord->aplay transitions.
    - Wire new test into tests/run-suite.mjs under 'full' suite.
    - Update docs/sb16-golden-sequence.md §9 note on ALSA 0xD5 teardown behavior.

